==============================================================================================
 MG-BASELINE: is the cluster-member infall-phase spread MG=0 for THIS channel?  (both foot.)
==============================================================================================

[A] INSTANTANEOUS-EFE vs HISTORY-EFE  (does a TIME-VARYING potential leak history into MG?)
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  symbolic: MG member accel = g(x(t)); the sourced field carries NO d/dt(worldline) label.
            => the CURRENT-position boost is memoryless; infall HISTORY drops out exactly.
  numeric : settled vs deep-plunger member at the SAME current radius -> IDENTICAL MG boost
            (both footings).  MG infall-phase spread at fixed TRUE 3D position = 0, exactly.
            [MI contrast: boost = f(y-history) along the worldline -> the 6-13% spread.]

[B] RETARDATION  (finite gravity/light crossing of a time-varying cluster potential)
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  sigma_cl=  1037 km/s ; t_cross(r/c)=2.06e+14s ; t_dyn(r/sigma)=5.95e+16s
  retardation fraction ~ v/c = 3.46e-03  (mean-field lag, O(1e-3)).
  CRUCIAL: retardation is in the SOURCE past light-cone, felt IDENTICALLY by every member at
  (x,t).  It shifts the MEAN field (~1e-3 in d) but carries no per-member orbit label ->
  infall-phase FAMILY spread stays EXACTLY 0.  (Contrast MI: kernel K(Box_u) retards along
  the TRACER'S OWN worldline -> per-orbit.)  Retardation cannot mimic the MI channel.

[C] PROJECTION MIMIC  (bin by observed radius, not true 3D -> false MG infall-phase spread?)
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Threat: at fixed PROJECTED radius, radial plungers sit at systematically different TRUE 3D
  radius than settled members -> different TRUE g_ext -> different MG boost d_MG(r_true).
  Since the infall-phase proxy correlates with orbit class, MG's real RADIAL trend aliases
  into the phase direction = a FALSE spread that mimics MI.  Quantify vs MI 6-13%.

  footing=canonical a0=9.360e-11   MI infall-phase band = 6.2-11.8%
    bin by TRUE 3D r (perfect deproj)         : mimic =  0.090%   <- theorem: ~0
    bin by R_proj    (NO deprojection, worst) : mimic =  2.249%
    bin by stat-deprojected r (class-blind)   : mimic =  2.185%
    -> raw projection mimic is 19% of the MI band TOP; after deproj 35% of the MI band FLOOR.

  footing=alternate a0=1.130e-10   MI infall-phase band = 7.5-14.1%
    bin by TRUE 3D r (perfect deproj)         : mimic =  0.108%   <- theorem: ~0
    bin by R_proj    (NO deprojection, worst) : mimic =  2.351%
    bin by stat-deprojected r (class-blind)   : mimic =  2.304%
    -> raw projection mimic is 17% of the MI band TOP; after deproj 31% of the MI band FLOOR.

[D] INTERLOPER / BACKSPLASH MIMIC  (non-members feel a different g_ext; if phase-tagged...)
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Interlopers = foreground/background galaxies projected into the cluster.  They feel a WEAK
  field g_ext (large true r or true field regime) -> HIGH isolated MOND boost (large d).  If
  they are preferentially tagged 'infalling' (large R_proj / high |v_los|), they inject a
  class-correlated d offset = a false MG spread.  Quantify vs the caustic-membership residual.

  footing=canonical   MI band 6.2-11.8%   (baseline projection mimic 2.249%)
    interloper fraction    5% (all mis-tagged infalling) : false spread =  0.247%   (2% of MI top)
    interloper fraction   15% (all mis-tagged infalling) : false spread =  1.278%   (11% of MI top)
    interloper fraction   30% (all mis-tagged infalling) : false spread =  4.427%   (38% of MI top)
    NOTE: this is the UNCUT worst case (100% of interlopers mis-tagged as infalling).
    The frozen estimator's caustic membership + Dressler-Shectman cut removes DS-coherent
    infalling groups (banked: fake-3sigma rate 28% -> 0.08% WITH the cut) and clips the
    caustic-outlier interlopers; residual interloper fraction after cuts ~1-3%, not 15-30%.

  footing=alternate   MI band 7.5-14.1%   (baseline projection mimic 2.351%)
    interloper fraction    5% (all mis-tagged infalling) : false spread =  0.276%   (2% of MI top)
    interloper fraction   15% (all mis-tagged infalling) : false spread =  1.424%   (10% of MI top)
    interloper fraction   30% (all mis-tagged infalling) : false spread =  4.670%   (33% of MI top)
    NOTE: this is the UNCUT worst case (100% of interlopers mis-tagged as infalling).
    The frozen estimator's caustic membership + Dressler-Shectman cut removes DS-coherent
    infalling groups (banked: fake-3sigma rate 28% -> 0.08% WITH the cut) and clips the
    caustic-outlier interlopers; residual interloper fraction after cuts ~1-3%, not 15-30%.

==============================================================================================
 SYNTHESIS  --  is MG=0 airtight for the cluster-member infall-phase channel?
==============================================================================================
 * AT FIXED TRUE 3D EXTERNAL FIELD: MG=0 is a THEOREM (banked mg_zero.py, re-verified [A]).
   MG is MEMORYLESS -- the current-position boost drops the infall history exactly; a time-
   varying potential [A] and retardation [B] shift the MEAN field but add ZERO family spread.
 * BUT THE OBSERVED SPREAD IN AN MG UNIVERSE IS NOT ZERO.  Two observational channels
   manufacture a false MG infall-phase spread:
     (C) PROJECTION: binning by projected radius aliases MG's real radial g_ext trend into
         the infall-phase direction (plungers sit at different true r than settled members
         at matched projected radius).  RAW mimic is a LARGE fraction of the MI band; class-
         blind statistical deprojection cuts it but a residual survives.
     (D) INTERLOPERS: field-boosted non-members mis-tagged infalling inject a class offset;
         uncut this reaches the MI band, but caustic membership + the DS cut suppress it.
 * THEREFORE the '<=0.3 dex deprojected a_ext binning + DS cut + caustic membership' frozen
   in the estimator (GAP_STATEMENT E2/E5) are NOT optional polish -- they are what turns the
   airtight-at-true-r theorem into an airtight-in-observation baseline.  A detection that
   skips them measures projection + interlopers, NOT modified inertia.
 * MG=0 is a THEOREM for the sourced-field channel at fixed true g_ext; it is a mitigation-
   DEPENDENT baseline in projection.  The residual mimic after the frozen cuts is the real
   MG floor the MI 6-13% must clear -- quantified above, both footings.
 * SCOPE: MI-CLASS (any history-dependent inertia) vs MG.  NOT framework-vs-Milgrom-linear.
   a0 value + s=-1 remain postulates.  Magnitude band is kernel-hostage.

EXIT 0
